            </zone>
            <zone h='94476' id='7' param='horz' type-v2='layout-flow' w='98888' x='556' y='4762'>
              <zone fixed-size='160' h='94476' id='6' is-fixed='true' param='vert' type-v2='layout-flow' w='98888' x='556' y='4762' />
            </zone>
          </zone>
          <zone-style>
            <format attr='border-color' value='#444444' />
            <format attr='border-style' value='none' />
            <format attr='border-width' value='0' />
            <format attr='margin' value='8' />
          </zone-style>
        </zone>
        <zone h='37143' id='3' name='Scenario - Loss Probability' w='97222' x='1111' y='7333' />
        <zone h='40000' id='9' name='AMZN | Five-Year Tail Risk Under Volatility Stress' w='97222' x='1597' y='46762' />
        <zone forceUpdate='true' h='10286' id='11' type-v2='text' w='98264' x='1389' y='87810'>
          <formatted-text>
            <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='12'>Methodology:</run>
            <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='12'> Five-year GBM Monte Carlo simulation with 1,000 paths per scenario. Historical daily volatility is scaled by 1.0× (Base), 1.5× (High Volatility), and 2.0× (Stress), while daily log-return drift, initial price, forecast horizon, and random seed remain constant.</run>
            <run>Æ&#10;</run>
            <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='12'>Key Finding:</run>
            <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='12'> Increasing volatility from 1.0× to 2.0× raises the probability of loss from 15.60% to 30.60%, while 5% Expected Shortfall worsens from −57.90% to −91.81%. Although mean terminal price increases, downside exposure rises substantially.</run>
          </formatted-text>
        </zone>
      </zones>
